When streaming tool calls, it seems like `input` can be undefined (when the tool call starts but before inputs actually start streaming in), but the types don't handle this case.

So if you do:
```
switch (toolPart.state) {
  case "input-streaming": {
    // this will crash when toolPart.input is undefined, but typescript doesn't complain
    const foo = toolPart.input.foo;
    ...
    break;
  }
  ...
}
```
